---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Kenzap"
  description="Privacy policy for the Kenzap website and Kenzap Nesting App."
  lang="en"
>
  <main class="privacy-page">
    <section class="privacy-shell">
      <a class="back-link" href="/">Back to Kenzap</a>
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</div>
      <h1>Privacy Policy for the Kenzap website and Kenzap Nesting App</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        This Privacy Policy explains what information may be processed when you use the Kenzap
        website and the Kenzap Nesting App. The app processes DXF files and nesting jobs locally.
        It may process limited technical information when you choose to send a crash report or
        contact Kenzap for support.
      </p>

      <div class="meta">Last updated: September 2, 2026</div>

      <section>
        <h2>1. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy applies to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>the Kenzap marketing website and related localized pages,</li>
          <li>the Kenzap Nesting App desktop application, and</li>
          <li>direct contact with us through the email addresses or external profiles linked on the website.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Website data</h2>
        <p>
          The website is primarily informational. We do not require account registration to browse it.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you visit the website, standard technical information may be processed by the hosting
          infrastructure or your browser, such as IP address, browser type, device information,
          timestamps, requested pages, and basic request logs. This data is typically used for site
          delivery, reliability, and security.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you contact us by email, LinkedIn, GitHub, YouTube, or another linked third-party service,
          we may receive the information you choose to share with us through those services.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you use the support form on this website, the submission is processed through Netlify
          Forms. In that case, the information you enter in the form, along with related technical
          metadata required to deliver and protect the form submission, may be processed by Netlify.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Kenzap Nesting App data</h2>
        <p>
          Kenzap Nesting App is a desktop application intended to process nesting jobs locally on the
          user’s machine.
        </p>
        <p>
          DXF files, nesting projects, job history, and other working data are handled locally on
          your device and are not intentionally transmitted to Kenzap as part of the app's core
          functionality. The app does not require a Kenzap cloud account or use behavioral analytics.
        </p>
        <p>
          The app creates limited diagnostic session logs and crash dumps locally by default. These
          records help identify startup failures, crashes, and problems with bundled helper processes.
          They remain on your device unless you choose to send or otherwise share them with Kenzap.
        </p>
        <p>
          Automatic transmission of crash reports is disabled by default. If the app detects that a
          crash occurred, it may ask on the next launch whether you want to send the report. No report
          is sent unless you choose to send it or have previously enabled automatic crash reporting.
          You may decline without affecting the app's core functionality.
        </p>
        <p>
          A crash report sent to Kenzap through Netlify may include a crash minidump, app and Electron
          versions, operating system, processor architecture, process type, crash identifier, IP
          address, and submission timestamp. This information is used only to diagnose crashes,
          improve reliability, and investigate security issues.
        </p>
        <p>
          Crash reports are not intended to include DXF files, nesting projects, or job history.
          However, because a minidump records limited application memory at the time of a crash, it
          may incidentally contain small fragments of information that were present in memory.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          The current website implementation is not intended to provide user accounts or in-app
          behavioral tracking. However, basic browser, hosting, or third-party service behavior may
          still involve technical storage or network logging necessary to load pages and external links.
        </p>
        <p>
          The support form also uses spam-protection measures including Netlify reCAPTCHA. Depending on
          how the service is delivered, Netlify and reCAPTCHA providers may process device, browser,
          network, and interaction data to help distinguish legitimate submissions from automated abuse.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          The website links to or relies on third-party services including Netlify, GitHub, LinkedIn,
          YouTube, and reCAPTCHA-related providers. If you interact with those services, their own
          privacy policies and terms apply.
        </p>
        <p>
          Netlify may process website support submissions and optional app crash reports on Kenzap's
          behalf. Microsoft may separately process Windows crash and reliability information according
          to your Windows privacy settings and Microsoft's applicable privacy terms.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We only expect to retain information that you voluntarily send to us, or technical records
          reasonably required for security, delivery, and support. Crash reports submitted to Kenzap,
          whether individually or through optional automatic reporting, are retained for no longer
          than 90 days, unless a longer period is reasonably needed to investigate an active reliability
          or security issue or comply with a legal obligation.
          Information you voluntarily submit for support is retained only as long as reasonably needed
          to respond and maintain relevant support records.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion,
          or restriction regarding personal data that relates to you. If you want to make such a
          request, withdraw consent to optional crash reporting, or ask a privacy-related question,
          contact us using the email below. You may decline a crash-report request and, when automatic
          reporting is available, disable it through the app settings.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy-related questions, contact:
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="mailto:support@kenzap.com">support@kenzap.com</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    :global(body) {
      background: #f6f7fc;
      color: #0a0a08;
      font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 300;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .privacy-page {
      min-height: 100vh;
      padding: 48px 24px 96px;
    }

    .privacy-shell {
      max-width: 820px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px;
      background: rgba(246, 247, 252, 0.92);
      border: 1px solid #dde1f0;
    }

    .back-link,
    .eyebrow,
    .meta {
      font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    }

    .back-link {
      display: inline-flex;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
      color: #4a4f5c;
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: color 0.2s;
    }

    .back-link:hover {
      color: #0a0a08;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: #1941df;
    }

    h1,
    h2 {
      font-family: 'Syne', sans-serif;
      letter-spacing: -0.02em;
      color: #0a0a08;
    }

    h1 {
      margin-bottom: 20px;
      font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 56px);
      line-height: 0.98;
    }

    .intro {
      margin-bottom: 16px;
      font-size: 18px;
      color: #4a4f5c;
    }

    .meta {
      margin-bottom: 40px;
      font-size: 11px;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: #8a9099;
    }

    section + section {
      margin-top: 32px;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    p,
    li {
      font-size: 15px;
      color: #4a4f5c;
    }

    p + p {
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    ul {
      margin: 12px 0 0 20px;
      padding: 0;
    }

    li + li {
      margin-top: 8px;
    }

    a {
      color: #0a0a08;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .privacy-page {
        padding: 24px 16px 72px;
      }

      .privacy-shell {
        padding: 32px 24px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
